      {
        "id": 52779,
        "name": "Zalrus9",
        "username": "Zalrus9",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/zalrus9/{size}/2124_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-02-06T03:13:08.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I think there's a theme with the Freedom Six in general, and that's consistancy. It seems like they're at thier best when luck is not on thier side (especially with Absolute Zero). One-armed Tempest is able to fish for those good cards in his deck (although he's a little slower that way), and G-Unity can get those golems out on a turn where she normally wouldn't. Even Wraith has the ability to deal damage if she's unable to do so becuase of a draw. Consistancy is certianly more key in this game, as there is no \"mulligan\" of any kind. &nbsp;The only one who is perhaps better is Team Leader Tachyon, but regular Tachyon can outdamage TLT in the long run</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I think even more importantly, the Freedom Six make sense thematically. Their lives suck, so they've adapted to a less than stellar way to keep them selves alive. Like Tempest's card says, it's the price of freedom.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Ah, that's my two cents. I do prefer most of the freedom Six because I don't like bad draws.</p>",
