      {
        "id": 52780,
        "name": "Sefirit",
        "username": "Sefirit",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/e68b1a/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-02-06T15:24:58.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Zalrus9\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/zalrus9/48/2124_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Zalrus9:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Ah, that's my two cents. I do prefer most of the freedom Six <strong>because I don't like bad draws</strong>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>My thoughts exactly!&nbsp; Getting stuck with a bad hand can really dampen the fun.&nbsp; With most card games I play I don't worry so much about making the deck as powerful as possible as much as making almost completely immune to bad luck. (Just my personal style.)&nbsp; If it doesn't work the way I want it to 90% of the time then I look to see if there is anyway to make it more consistent without loosing the point of the deck.&nbsp; Search and Draw are my two favorite things ever in any deck based game.</p>\n<p>Team leader Tachyon has become a favorite with my play group because she makes the experience more enjoyable for everyone playing.</p>",
