      {
        "id": 52782,
        "name": "Spiff",
        "username": "Spiff",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/{size}/1865_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-02-10T02:31:03.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>We played a game using Golem Unity (spend 4 hp to play a golem) and the optional rule where when a golem dies, you get 2 hp back. &nbsp;We quickly realized that 2 was too much, since once you got a few cards out and could play golems without having to spend hp to do it, you'd start getting more hp back from dead golems than you'd spent to play them. &nbsp;However, changing it to only getting 1 hp back from a dead golem actually made it feel just about perfect. &nbsp;You'd still think twice about having to spend 4 hp to play a golem, but you your little helpers were trying to keep you alive as you reabsorbed their little dead bodies back into you. &nbsp;I think we'll continue playing Golem Unity this way.</p>",
        "post_number": 25,
